    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d283">

                <pb facs="0489" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/557: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece (Morris) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-10-06T13:00:00+02:00">October 6, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 6—8:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>105. Your 48.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d283-f1"/> I made representations on October
                    1st. Foreign <pb facs="0490" n="400" xml:id="pg400"/> Office informs me verbally
                    that Venizelos is personally drafting a reply which I may expect to receive
                    within a few days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
